MultimediaType.description:
Gets or sets the Multimedia Type of the binary content.
            This only applies to the binary content of Multimedia Components;
            for templates with binary content, this property is always null.

SelectedWorkflowId.description:
Gets or sets the selected identifier of the {Tridion.TranslationManager.OpenApi.V3.Dto.TargetLanguage.SelectedWorkflow}.
If setting an identifier not present in {Tridion.TranslationManager.OpenApi.V3.Dto.TargetLanguage.AvailableWorkflowIds} the {Tridion.TranslationManager.OpenApi.V3.Dto.TargetLanguage.SelectedWorkflowId}
will be set to the first entry in {Tridion.TranslationManager.OpenApi.V3.Dto.TargetLanguage.AvailableWorkflowIds}.

Script.description:
Gets or sets the script of an automated Activity.
                An Activity Definition can represent an automated activity to which a script is associated.
                This script is then executed by the TCM Workflow Agent once the workflow process reaches the activity.
            
                When you create a Process Definition, you can define an automatic Activity Definition simply by setting
                the Script property. You don't need to explicitly specify the "ActivityDefinition.Assignee", it will be
                automatically set to the TCM Workflow Agent during the creation of the Process Definition.
            
                The TCM Workflow Agent user is declared in the TCM configuration in the workflow section as the following example illustrates:
                
                    &lt;configuration&gt;
                        &lt;workflow workflowAgentAccountUri="tcm:0-3-65552" /&gt;
                    &lt;/configuration&gt;
